{
  "name": "hold_knife",
  "note": "(anim-rework S6 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced; M5) The lethal takedown from the hold, a 3.0 s one-shot keyed at guard_knife_collapse's frames (0, 1, 3, 5, 8, 11, 15, 20, 25, 29, 40, 47 of 48; phase min(t / 3, 1) x 47 / 48): short and not gratuitous: 0-0.2 s the knife hand draws about 6 cm back across his throat toward his right while the left arm clamps him and her chest pulls back; 0.2-0.35 s held; at 0.35 s she lets go as he stiffens and folds forward away from her: her hands come off, she eases back to a low ready (pelvis 4 cm further back, knees soft), the knife hand low by her right thigh, the left by her side; still from about 1 s with the breath. No flourish, no follow-through. Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in); wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. The arms were solved onto the guard's contacts (his clips posed at the game's hold placement: 0.32 m ahead, 0.1 m to her left, his 1.78 m against her 1.68 m) and written as plain angles: edit these numbers directly. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
